{
  "case_id": "2001-00-758",
  "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court record",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Postal Service (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For decades Federal employers and the Merit Systems Protection Board have engaged in the common sense practice of considering an employee's prior disciplinary record in deciding what punishment is appropriate for subsequent misconduct. The settled practice has long been to do so, even when a prior disciplinary action is subject to a pending labor grievance, although in that context, the board permits the employee to collaterally attack the prior actions in proceedings before it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: If there is a collateral attack, the employee says, look, I filed a grievance and it's pending, what then is the burden of proof by the Government employer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But what -- what is it with regard to the prior offenses, if you will, that have -- for which grievance procedures have been filed? How is that then addressed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the issue that -- that remains open is the question of what effect the grievance that has been set aside should have on the board's decision affirming the removal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unknown)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: Why is the remand necessary? What -- if we agree with -- with you on the merits, what -- what remains to be decided by the Federal circuit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We -- we think that the fairest reading of the court of appeals decision, as it applies both to Federal employers and the Merit Systems Protection Board, the holding of the court is unqualified. It says that consideration may not be given to these prior actions as long as there are grievances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the board's regulations permit the board to reopen any case at any time to reconsider it in light of a grievance which may have proved successful."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the respondent's basic position and the Federal circuit's basic position is predicated on the notion that prior disciplinary actions are unreliable and that Federal employers act in bad faith when they impose discipline."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Statute",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "5 U.S.C., section 7701(c)(1)(B), which is copied at page 51 in the appendix to the petition, provides that the decision of the agency shall be sustained -- and that is by the MSPB -- only if the agency's decision is supported by a preponderance of the evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0007",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Government did not respond to any of respondent's arguments in the court of appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that there are two things wrong with the way the MSPB does -- does -- treats prior disciplinary actions. One is it ignores the statutory burden of proof standard, section 7701(c)(1)(B)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Case Law",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0001-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under Douglas v. Veterans Administration, the MSPB in any given case will conduct a -- an inquiry to ensure that the penalty fits the crime, so to speak. It will make sure that the punishment is not disproportional, is not unreasonable, and so on and so forth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brands",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the prior is being grieved, the Government's decision does not get any deference. It -- the Government always bears the burden."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Did you challenge the Bolling rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brands",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think there's no presumption of regularity because when the action comes before the board or before an arbitrator itself, it is not entitled to any presumption of regularity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But why did -- but when you answer the question, would you tell us why it would make any difference whether it is -- whether there's the collateral proceeding going on, whether there's a direct attack going on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brands",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government action, if it is taken to the MSPB, is not entitled to any deference at all because the Government bears the burden of proving de novo that what happened actually occurred."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brands",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, it's an argument that's raised for the first time today here at the lectern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But it does -- it does weaken your argument that the Government serves its purpose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brands",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The short answer is no, if the allegation is that those are disciplinary grievances. There are 126,000 cases pending, but the vast majority of those are contract grievances and not disciplinary grievances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, Mr. Garre. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2001-00-758",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3cf403228b6396ab02cc988ede640a66c29f890d9f446d1ab2406aa797ef1478",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3cf403228b63-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, to follow up on a question by Justice Kennedy, I want to make clear that we would not object to the continuance of the grievance."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
